WEBVTT

00:00:45.737 --> 00:00:48.865
- I don't get why you brush your buggalo.
They have no hair.

00:00:48.865 --> 00:00:50.826
Shh! They don't know that.

00:00:50.826 --> 00:00:52.995
Don't know what?

00:00:52.995 --> 00:00:55.288
- They're just such beautiful creatures.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.624
My parents own the largest herd on Mars.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.751
Where do you keep them all?

00:00:59.751 --> 00:01:02.629
O-M-Jah!
Don't know how I missed them!

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.047
- We raise them for food

00:01:04.047 --> 00:01:07.009
but Betsy here has been my pet
since I was a kid.

00:01:07.009 --> 00:01:08.427
That's why we not eat her!

00:01:08.427 --> 00:01:09.761
Yet.

00:01:09.761 --> 00:01:11.513
- Don't know how I missed you either!

00:01:11.513 --> 00:01:14.141
- Amy, you forget the best part
of raising buggalo.

00:01:14.141 --> 00:01:15.392
Bugfighting season!

00:01:15.392 --> 00:01:17.519
flamenco sting

00:01:17.519 --> 00:01:18.645
- Neat!

00:01:19.855 --> 00:01:22.691
- Nobody's gonna fight
sweet little Betsy, are they?

00:01:22.691 --> 00:01:24.484
- No, no. Females too wimpy.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.570
Buggalo matadors only fight the males.

00:01:28.071 --> 00:01:30.615
How do I keep
missing these things?!

00:01:30.615 --> 00:01:33.535
- Nobody should be fighting
any kind of buggalo.

00:01:33.535 --> 00:01:35.412
It's cruel and inhumanoid.

00:01:35.412 --> 00:01:37.914
- Oh, please.
They're just brainless insects.

00:01:37.914 --> 00:01:41.418
- Really? 'Cause they have
very large brain pans

00:01:41.418 --> 00:01:43.462
according to the brain-ometer.

00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:44.963
- Big don't mean smart.

00:01:44.963 --> 00:01:48.258
Zoidberg's big, but he got
the intelligence of a brine shrimp.

00:01:48.258 --> 00:01:49.843
- Thank you, sir!

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.762
- It's not about intelligence.

00:01:51.762 --> 00:01:54.639
There's just something...
special about them.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.518
- Ew, gross!

00:02:00.103 --> 00:02:02.356
- After lunch, you all come downtown.

00:02:02.356 --> 00:02:05.817
We kick off bugfighting season
with the running of the buggalo!

00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:07.110
- Sounds dangerous.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.112
- Oh, no. Couple people get killed.

00:02:09.112 --> 00:02:10.906
Not many. Not dangerous at all.

00:02:10.906 --> 00:02:12.407
- People get killed, you say?

00:02:12.407 --> 00:02:14.826
- Four, five tops. Plus some robots.

00:02:14.826 --> 00:02:17.329
- But mostly people, you say?
I'll do it.

00:02:17.329 --> 00:02:19.498
Let's run it!

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:21.792
- You guys can't be serious!

00:02:21.792 --> 00:02:24.711
Leela, you're not gonna
participate in this, are you?

00:02:26.254 --> 00:02:29.341
- Uh... How about
we let this be your issue?

00:02:32.302 --> 00:02:34.513
Welcome, spectators, runners,

00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:36.181
and coffin salesmen,

00:02:36.181 --> 00:02:39.309
to the annual running
of the buggalo!

00:02:40.811 --> 00:02:43.188
We got a great group of buggalo...

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:47.234
...and a lazy-looking bunch of runners.

00:02:49.027 --> 00:02:52.823
So sign those liability waivers,
say goodbye to your loved ones...

00:02:52.823 --> 00:02:55.325
And run for your lives!

00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:01.081
And they're off and running!

00:03:01.081 --> 00:03:04.209
Hello, splatter fans.
Don Cunningham here.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:06.420
The red planet will run red today

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.339
with the blood of its bravest heroes.

00:03:09.339 --> 00:03:10.632
Also their guts.

00:03:28.358 --> 00:03:29.943
Whoo!

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.738
- Next time, watch where you're going!

00:03:36.074 --> 00:03:37.659
And the buggalo make the turn

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:39.745
towards the Mars Vegas Strip,

00:03:39.745 --> 00:03:42.664
home of the $1.99 subprime rib.

00:03:42.664 --> 00:03:45.834
Come on! Baby needs a new left hip!

00:04:03.852 --> 00:04:06.730
Man, I'm running outta steam.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.774
Good thing that's not what I run on.

00:04:18.325 --> 00:04:21.411
I'm Bender, baby!
What's your name?

00:04:21.411 --> 00:04:25.582
- Marquita Maria Christina
Chiquita Alana Paloma...

00:04:25.582 --> 00:04:29.336
- Uh-huh... Right... Okay...
- ...Ramona Rosita Catalina Lupe

00:04:29.336 --> 00:04:33.006
Lunes Martes Miercoles
Jueves Viernes Sabado Domingo...

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:34.508
- Cat's got some moves!

00:04:34.508 --> 00:04:37.469
- He's very light on his feet
for a two-ton robot.

00:04:37.469 --> 00:04:39.429
- I've never seen such beauty.

00:04:39.429 --> 00:04:41.223
Do you have many more names?

00:04:41.223 --> 00:04:44.559
- Yes, many. Veronica Helena Hermina...
- Uh-huh? Right.

00:04:44.559 --> 00:04:46.687
- ...Francesca Esperanza Valentina...
- Okay. Keep going.

00:04:46.687 --> 00:04:50.232
...Carmelita Leonora
Lupita Isabella Juanita

00:04:50.232 --> 00:04:53.110
Teresa Sofia Mariana Benihana Bonita

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.112
Nereida Guadalupe

00:04:55.112 --> 00:04:56.321
Alvarez.

00:05:07.457 --> 00:05:09.459
No! Where'd she go?!

00:05:11.378 --> 00:05:14.548
I'll never see
the love of my life again!

00:05:14.548 --> 00:05:16.174
And even more tragic,

00:05:16.174 --> 00:05:18.260
she'll never see me again!

00:05:21.972 --> 00:05:23.974
Another magnificent running of the buggalo

00:05:23.974 --> 00:05:26.143
has come to an end.

00:05:26.143 --> 00:05:28.729
Along with many, many lives.

00:05:28.729 --> 00:05:32.190
What a sick and unnecessary exercise.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.359
And such a beautiful tradition.

00:05:35.986 --> 00:05:37.487
Excuse me, Señor Bender?

00:05:37.487 --> 00:05:39.865
- I'm Abner Doubledeal.
- I know you!

00:05:39.865 --> 00:05:42.701
You're the commissioner of
the Ultimate Robot Fighting League.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.244
And also every other league.

00:05:44.244 --> 00:05:48.206
- Plus, I'm El Comisario of
La Asociación de Bugfighting.

00:05:48.206 --> 00:05:50.917
And I need you to be my new matador.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:53.420
Wh-What happened to the old matador?

00:05:54.671 --> 00:05:57.049
- Uh, he retired.
- I don't know.

00:05:57.049 --> 00:05:59.926
It seems dangerous.
I mean, I know I'm great,

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.928
but do you think
I'm great enough?

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:04.556
- Definitely not.
That's why you'll need to be trained

00:06:04.556 --> 00:06:06.558
by the greatest matador alive.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.522
Marquita Maria Christina, etc.?

00:06:12.522 --> 00:06:16.902
I would die a thousand deaths
to spend one minute with her!

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:20.238
- Then you have chosen
the right line of work!

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.086
- Marquita's the best.

00:06:34.086 --> 00:06:36.296
You'll wanna learn
all her trademark moves.

00:06:36.296 --> 00:06:38.924
- Trademark infringement?
My specialty!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:50.811
Ooh, and Matador Marquita
dispatches the honorable beast

00:06:50.811 --> 00:06:52.437
with utmost honor.

00:06:52.437 --> 00:06:55.023
I've never seen so much honor, folks.

00:06:55.023 --> 00:06:58.986
I just hope Marquita
doesn't slip on all that honor.

00:07:01.446 --> 00:07:03.532
- Bender, I want you
to meet your trainer.

00:07:03.532 --> 00:07:06.493
Matador Marquita Maria Christina
something something.

00:07:06.493 --> 00:07:10.330
- ¡Comisario! If you can't remember
a simple name, I'm not--

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.289
- I remember it!

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:15.043
Chiquita Alana Paloma
Ramona Rosita Catalina Lupe Lunes...

00:07:15.043 --> 00:07:17.796
- Just train him to survive this season.
I gotta go.

00:07:17.796 --> 00:07:19.798
The NFL's up for sale on Craigslist.

00:07:19.798 --> 00:07:21.800
- ...Valentina Carmelita Lenora...

00:07:23.051 --> 00:07:25.846
- You remember that
from our brief meeting?

00:07:25.846 --> 00:07:26.847
- Alvarez.

00:07:26.847 --> 00:07:30.475
I pay close attention when
things are about to get jiggy.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.814
- I too was struck by the thunderbolt
of love at first sight.

00:07:36.773 --> 00:07:39.026
But love must wait until you have studied

00:07:39.026 --> 00:07:41.028
the ways of the bugfighter.

00:07:41.028 --> 00:07:43.572
- First study, then jiggy?

00:07:43.572 --> 00:07:46.867
- Patience is the hallmark of the matador.

00:07:48.577 --> 00:07:52.539
We shall begin with the most
important element of bugfighting.

00:07:52.539 --> 00:07:54.750
- Stabbing? Screaming?

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:55.751
Jigging?

00:07:55.751 --> 00:07:57.294
- Clothing.

00:08:00.922 --> 00:08:03.300
- Uh, you got anything slimming?

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.386
I wanna give the buggalo
as small a target as possible.

00:08:06.386 --> 00:08:09.056
- Sir! My family has been
making matador outfits

00:08:09.056 --> 00:08:10.515
for seven generations!

00:08:10.515 --> 00:08:12.267
- So you're experienced?

00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:15.270
- My father died yesterday.
You're my first customer.

00:08:16.438 --> 00:08:19.316
Honestly, most of
our matador work is repairs.

00:08:19.316 --> 00:08:21.777
Lots and lots of repairs.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.262
- Ah, ah. Only if you
survive your first bugfight.

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:51.056
And maybe gargle something.

00:08:51.056 --> 00:08:52.057
trumpet sting

00:08:52.057 --> 00:08:55.644
- In honor of Bender's
first bugfight tomorrow,

00:08:55.644 --> 00:08:59.314
Buggalo wings with
Martian Valley Ranch!

00:08:59.314 --> 00:09:01.400
- Them's good eats!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.277
- I can't believe you're going
through with this, Bender.

00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:05.988
They're just innocent bugs.

00:09:05.988 --> 00:09:08.323
- And yet, you're eating one right now.

00:09:08.323 --> 00:09:11.702
- No, I'm not. This is Beyond Buggalo.

00:09:11.702 --> 00:09:14.454
- Yuck. What it made from, plant?

00:09:14.454 --> 00:09:17.457
- No. Pork! I never did like pigs.

00:09:17.457 --> 00:09:20.043
Betsy? Want some porky-worky?

00:09:21.503 --> 00:09:23.046
- Hey! Why you talking to her?

00:09:23.046 --> 00:09:25.007
Dumb bugs can't understand anything!

00:09:25.007 --> 00:09:28.510
- Now, now, Leo.
Perhaps Amy has a point.

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.303
I brought my X-ray specs

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:33.306
so I can directly examine Betsy's brain.

00:09:34.975 --> 00:09:37.102
My word!

00:09:37.102 --> 00:09:40.313
Amy is absolutely 100%...

00:09:40.313 --> 00:09:41.314
wrong.

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:44.234
Buggalo heads are literally empty!

00:09:44.234 --> 00:09:46.486
They have no brain whatsoever!

00:09:46.486 --> 00:09:50.282
- Maybe not, but Betsy's
got emotional intelligence!

00:09:50.282 --> 00:09:52.784
- That's the stupidest
kind of intelligence!

00:09:55.954 --> 00:09:57.956
rousing mariachi trumpet playing

00:10:04.963 --> 00:10:07.382
I love you, Bender!

00:10:07.382 --> 00:10:08.884
- Shut up, señorita! I know it!

00:10:09.885 --> 00:10:12.179
- Marry me, Bender! Then, divorce me!

00:10:12.179 --> 00:10:13.930
- Man, this is my kind of sport.

00:10:16.141 --> 00:10:17.434
Oh, right. The buggalo.

00:10:19.269 --> 00:10:21.104
Eh, you don't look so fierce.

00:10:22.773 --> 00:10:24.358
Oh, that's new.

00:10:24.358 --> 00:10:27.402
- Bender! Remember what I taught you!

00:10:27.402 --> 00:10:30.697
Always smooth
your compression socks.

00:10:30.697 --> 00:10:32.115
- Ah, right.

00:10:42.501 --> 00:10:44.544
- Oh no! My cerveza hat!

00:10:44.544 --> 00:10:46.338
dramatic music building

00:10:50.842 --> 00:10:52.344
And the crowd falls silent

00:10:52.344 --> 00:10:54.763
as one of their own
faces mortal peril.

00:10:58.266 --> 00:11:00.560
- Save him, Matador Bender!

00:11:01.895 --> 00:11:04.648
They're on the edge
of their seats, waiting to hear how I,

00:11:04.648 --> 00:11:07.651
Don Cunningham,
describe the ensuing carnage.

00:11:11.113 --> 00:11:13.323
Fry! No!

00:11:13.323 --> 00:11:15.325
- It's okay! Five-second rule!

00:11:22.833 --> 00:11:26.169
- Astounding! Matador Bender
has won the audience over!

00:11:26.169 --> 00:11:29.464
Fembots are tossing
their dainties into the ring.

00:11:29.464 --> 00:11:32.092
- They're throwing their
shiny metal asses at me?

00:11:32.092 --> 00:11:34.594
- I love you, Bender.

00:11:43.937 --> 00:11:45.522
The tension is excruciating!

00:11:45.522 --> 00:11:48.817
You don't wanna miss
one second of this action, fans!

00:11:48.817 --> 00:11:50.861
And now, a word from our sponsor.

00:11:51.987 --> 00:11:55.240
- As a matador who may
or may not still be alive,

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:58.201
I know nothing's more
annoying than a bugfight

00:11:58.201 --> 00:12:00.704
getting interrupted
by a commercial.

00:12:00.704 --> 00:12:04.333
So upgrade now
to ad-free Fulu Premium.

00:12:04.333 --> 00:12:07.586
The same old shows
for an exciting new price.

00:12:14.126 --> 00:12:15.502
Welcome back, fans.

00:12:15.502 --> 00:12:18.088
What a beautiful afternoon at the arena

00:12:18.088 --> 00:12:22.050
where Matador Bender is about
to be shredded like tin foil.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:25.595
dramatic music building

00:12:32.227 --> 00:12:34.563
Bender, did I teach you nothing?

00:12:34.563 --> 00:12:35.606
- Kinda!

00:12:42.195 --> 00:12:45.699
I'm dead if I can't magically
pull a sword outta my ass.

00:12:45.699 --> 00:12:47.034
Hey, wait!

00:12:53.332 --> 00:12:56.251
- I'm in my car now, on the way home.
But what's this?

00:12:56.251 --> 00:12:58.503
I hear the crowd roaring behind me.

00:13:08.472 --> 00:13:12.392
- Matador Bender, in honor of
your thrilling come-from-behind victory,

00:13:12.392 --> 00:13:15.771
I award you the head and carapace
of your defeated rival...

00:13:18.649 --> 00:13:20.692
...in lieu of financial remuneration.

00:13:48.011 --> 00:13:51.098
- Ooh! This cart has buggalo legs!

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.852
You did well, Bender.

00:13:55.852 --> 00:13:58.105
Of all the students
I have ever taught,

00:13:58.105 --> 00:14:00.065
you are the one who is alive.

00:14:00.065 --> 00:14:02.609
- Hey, Marquita,
let me ask you something,

00:14:02.609 --> 00:14:04.361
matador to matador.

00:14:04.361 --> 00:14:06.863
- "Hay" is for horses. Go on.

00:14:06.863 --> 00:14:08.156
- Do you think it's possible

00:14:08.156 --> 00:14:11.243
buggalo really do have
some kind of awareness?

00:14:11.243 --> 00:14:14.288
'Cause when it looked me in the eye,
I felt something.

00:14:14.288 --> 00:14:16.164
Not something phony like love.

00:14:16.164 --> 00:14:18.292
Something real like the Force.

00:14:18.292 --> 00:14:20.460
- I too have felt such a thing.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:22.838
But, of course, it is impossible for a bug

00:14:22.838 --> 00:14:25.299
to feel the complex emotions

00:14:25.299 --> 00:14:26.800
we robots feel.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.885
- Speaking of complex emotions,

00:14:28.885 --> 00:14:32.639
how are you feeling about the jiggy
we earlier discussed gettin'?

00:14:49.364 --> 00:14:51.700
music building

00:15:01.418 --> 00:15:03.378
- It's a soothing sound, isn't it?

00:15:03.378 --> 00:15:06.715
- Amy!
- You scared me brickless!

00:15:06.715 --> 00:15:09.176
- I was just tucking Betsy in.

00:15:09.176 --> 00:15:10.844
Anyway, congrats.

00:15:10.844 --> 00:15:12.387
I'm no bugfighting fan

00:15:12.387 --> 00:15:14.681
but you must feel great after today.

00:15:14.681 --> 00:15:17.309
- I always feel great.
'Cause I am.

00:15:17.309 --> 00:15:20.187
But, I also feel something else tonight.

00:15:20.187 --> 00:15:22.481
Something I've never felt before.

00:15:22.481 --> 00:15:24.274
- Guilt?
- Maybe.

00:15:24.274 --> 00:15:26.568
I always wondered what guilt felt like.

00:15:26.568 --> 00:15:29.237
Hey, um, can I come in?

00:15:29.237 --> 00:15:31.698
They're too dumb to know
I killed their pal, right?

00:15:31.698 --> 00:15:33.617
Probably.

00:15:33.617 --> 00:15:35.452
Just stay away from Betsy.

00:15:36.203 --> 00:15:38.789
flamenco guitar flourish

00:15:40.916 --> 00:15:44.086
I'm sorry I killed your friend.

00:15:44.086 --> 00:15:46.672
Or uncle. Or fruncle.

00:15:46.672 --> 00:15:49.466
Can you forgive me?

00:15:53.679 --> 00:15:56.598
It really is such a soothing sound.

00:15:57.349 --> 00:15:58.892
Bender...

00:15:59.476 --> 00:16:01.103
Bender...

00:16:01.812 --> 00:16:03.689
Bender!

00:16:03.689 --> 00:16:06.566
- What? Who's there?
Is that you, Fruncle Friender?

00:16:06.566 --> 00:16:08.402
We are honored

00:16:08.402 --> 00:16:10.612
to share our sleeping space with you.

00:16:10.612 --> 00:16:13.240
You can talk?!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.909
I mean, not as good as me can, but still.

00:16:15.909 --> 00:16:18.328
Please make yourself comfortable

00:16:18.328 --> 00:16:20.163
in the place of honor

00:16:20.163 --> 00:16:22.374
at the bottom of the sleeping pile.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.044
I can't breathe!

00:16:26.044 --> 00:16:29.464
Oh, right. Robots don't breathe.

00:16:29.464 --> 00:16:32.050
Actually, this is pretty cozy.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.593
flamenco guitar flourish

00:16:48.692 --> 00:16:50.068
- Guys, guys, guys, guys, guys!

00:16:52.321 --> 00:16:53.322
- What?

00:16:53.322 --> 00:16:56.450
- You're not gonna believe this,
but something amazing happened.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.619
The buggalo spoke to me!

00:16:58.619 --> 00:16:59.995
- That is amazing!

00:16:59.995 --> 00:17:01.997
And we don't believe you!

00:17:03.582 --> 00:17:05.000
- Which buggalo spoke?

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.168
- All of them!

00:17:06.168 --> 00:17:08.587
Buggalo can be singular or plural.

00:17:08.587 --> 00:17:10.213
- I understand, Bender.

00:17:10.213 --> 00:17:11.882
Buggalo cannot speak,

00:17:11.882 --> 00:17:14.468
but sometimes,
I feel as though they do.

00:17:14.468 --> 00:17:15.677
But they don't.

00:17:15.677 --> 00:17:18.347
- They do not don't! Tell her, Amy!

00:17:18.347 --> 00:17:19.640
- Uh, Bender,

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.601
I think you may have taken me
a little too literally.

00:17:22.601 --> 00:17:25.270
- Nuh-uh! They're intelligent creatures!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.439
I say the travesty of bugfighting

00:17:27.439 --> 00:17:29.608
must end once and for all!

00:17:29.608 --> 00:17:31.735
- Then it was nice having jiggy with you.

00:17:31.735 --> 00:17:33.904
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:17:33.904 --> 00:17:36.198
I must prepare for a bugfight.

00:17:36.198 --> 00:17:38.200
- Marquita! Don't go!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.034
Please!

00:17:40.118 --> 00:17:42.287
She seems nice.

00:17:50.879 --> 00:17:53.423
- Poor things. Don't worry.

00:17:53.423 --> 00:17:55.342
You'll be okay.

00:17:55.342 --> 00:17:57.469
No, you won't!

00:17:57.469 --> 00:18:00.681
I was lying! I'm sorry.

00:18:01.515 --> 00:18:03.433
- Guys, guys, I've got a plan.

00:18:03.433 --> 00:18:06.853
I'm gonna disguise myself
as El Gran Buggalo

00:18:06.853 --> 00:18:09.106
and put a stop to this savagery.

00:18:10.107 --> 00:18:11.942
I don't usually do the right thing,

00:18:11.942 --> 00:18:13.610
but I'll be ruining everyone's day,

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:14.987
so it balances out.

00:18:16.363 --> 00:18:19.283
Whoa, trippy. Now, here's the idea.

00:18:19.283 --> 00:18:21.326
Just at the key moment,

00:18:21.326 --> 00:18:23.787
I'll rip off my disguise and say...

00:18:28.125 --> 00:18:29.793
That oughta convince 'em.

00:18:31.295 --> 00:18:33.630
Today's match pits the greatest matador

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.048
of her generation

00:18:35.048 --> 00:18:37.050
against the greatest buggalo of its.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.177
You know him, you love him.

00:18:39.177 --> 00:18:41.096
El Gran Buggalo!

00:18:41.096 --> 00:18:43.265
Look how his legs barely move

00:18:43.265 --> 00:18:46.977
as he glides effortlessly,
with all the majesty and grace

00:18:46.977 --> 00:18:49.021
of a dog on a skateboard.

00:18:51.106 --> 00:18:54.276
Marquita, it's me.
Don't worry. I'm just gonna...

00:18:58.071 --> 00:19:01.617
What's this?
El Gran Buggalo is up on his hind legs.

00:19:01.617 --> 00:19:04.202
Is he trying to teach us a new dance?

00:19:04.202 --> 00:19:06.538
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:19:16.298 --> 00:19:18.759
Man, this head is
really stuck on tight.

00:19:18.759 --> 00:19:20.469
Oh crap!

00:19:20.469 --> 00:19:21.845
- Kill it already!

00:19:21.845 --> 00:19:24.514
It's not getting any tastier
just standing there!

00:19:30.646 --> 00:19:33.732
And Matador Marquita
moves in for the kill.

00:19:33.732 --> 00:19:35.233
It's all over, folks.

00:19:35.233 --> 00:19:38.195
This is Don "Beat the Traffic" Cunningham
signing off.

00:19:43.241 --> 00:19:45.827
Spanish guitar flourish

00:19:48.246 --> 00:19:49.247
guitar flourish

00:19:50.165 --> 00:19:51.541
dramatic sting

00:19:58.298 --> 00:20:00.801
Don't you people get it?!

00:20:00.801 --> 00:20:03.512
This buggalo is just an innocent...

00:20:03.929 --> 00:20:05.180
dramatic sting

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.390
...robot?

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.809
- How did you get that off so easily?

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:14.523
- Bender, no! Are you in pain?

00:20:14.523 --> 00:20:17.109
- Marquita, my darling. I'm...

00:20:17.109 --> 00:20:18.110
I'm okay.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.237
Luckily, the sword just
went through my head.

00:20:22.948 --> 00:20:26.368
People of Mars! Matadors!

00:20:26.368 --> 00:20:28.996
- Don Cunningham!
- He went home!

00:20:29.413 --> 00:20:32.416
- Maybe buggalo really are brainless.

00:20:32.416 --> 00:20:34.668
Maybe they don't feel any pain.

00:20:34.668 --> 00:20:37.754
Maybe they don't suffer.
But, even so,

00:20:37.754 --> 00:20:39.965
what does it say about us

00:20:39.965 --> 00:20:42.801
that we celebrate
their bloody deaths?

00:20:42.801 --> 00:20:44.970
Instead of celebrating death,

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.597
should we not be
celebrating life?

00:20:47.597 --> 00:20:49.516
And love?

00:20:49.516 --> 00:20:51.977
- Bender, hear me now.

00:20:51.977 --> 00:20:54.438
I... love... bugfighting.

00:20:54.438 --> 00:20:56.523
- You lousy tramp!
I oughta kick you!

00:20:56.523 --> 00:20:58.442
- But I love you more.

00:20:58.442 --> 00:20:59.651
- Okay, that's better.

00:20:59.651 --> 00:21:01.778
Let us end this barbaric,

00:21:01.778 --> 00:21:04.281
yet noble, yet barbaric ritual

00:21:04.281 --> 00:21:05.866
once and for all!

00:21:08.994 --> 00:21:10.621
Yet noble--
- Shh.

00:21:10.621 --> 00:21:13.165
- Guess you were right, Amy.
I'm proud of you.

00:21:13.165 --> 00:21:14.666
You disinherited.

00:21:15.667 --> 00:21:18.420
Buggalo fighting
now banned forever.

00:21:20.422 --> 00:21:23.175
But gambling still legal.
Nothing wrong with gambling.

00:21:23.175 --> 00:21:24.885
- I brought mines with me.

00:21:27.095 --> 00:21:30.057
- Come. Let us make the jiggy.

00:21:36.939 --> 00:21:38.857
We are the buggalo.

00:21:40.025 --> 00:21:42.486
- What?! They can talk?

00:21:45.155 --> 00:21:46.156
- My word!

00:21:46.156 --> 00:21:50.035
It seems that while each
individual buggalo is brainless,

00:21:50.035 --> 00:21:53.330
their empty skulls form resonance chambers

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:57.209
that allow large groups
to assemble a hive mind!

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.420
The raisin man is correct.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:02.339
We have consciousness,

00:22:02.339 --> 00:22:05.092
and we feel emotions.

00:22:05.092 --> 00:22:08.303
Fear, pain, suffering.

00:22:08.303 --> 00:22:10.222
All the emotions.

00:22:10.222 --> 00:22:12.015
But, most of all,

00:22:12.015 --> 00:22:13.976
we have a deep love

00:22:13.976 --> 00:22:16.061
of buggalo fighting!

00:22:17.104 --> 00:22:18.063
- Huh?
- Say what?

00:22:18.063 --> 00:22:20.857
Much of our culture is built around

00:22:20.857 --> 00:22:22.818
this ancient tradition.

00:22:22.818 --> 00:22:25.946
It's not a very rich culture,
we admit that.

00:22:25.946 --> 00:22:29.658
We just like to eat grass
and kill matadors.

00:22:29.658 --> 00:22:32.452
But, we refuse to forsake

00:22:32.452 --> 00:22:34.579
our noble traditions.

00:22:34.579 --> 00:22:37.332
The fight must continue!

00:22:43.213 --> 00:22:44.673
- I love you, Bender!

00:22:44.673 --> 00:22:47.926
We shall die together
with great honor.

00:22:47.926 --> 00:22:49.678
- I love you, too, baby.

00:22:50.512 --> 00:22:53.348
- But, Bender!
You said we was engaged!

00:22:53.348 --> 00:22:56.101
- No! He swore his love to me!

00:22:56.101 --> 00:22:57.352
- And me!

00:22:57.352 --> 00:22:59.813
- Bender. Are you two-timing me?!

00:22:59.813 --> 00:23:02.608
- Two? Nah, nah.
It's way more than that.

00:23:02.608 --> 00:23:05.360
- How did this happen? And when?

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:08.030
- Well, remember when
I said I spent a whole night

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:09.531
sleeping with the buggalo?

00:23:09.531 --> 00:23:12.117
It was actually only part of a night.

00:23:12.117 --> 00:23:13.910
And I didn't do much sleepin'.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:14.911
dramatic sting

00:23:14.911 --> 00:23:17.205
- I call first gore.

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:21.960
- Well, I deserve this.

00:23:26.214 --> 00:23:28.091
- This has been Don Cunningham.

00:23:28.091 --> 00:23:29.551
Goodnight, everybody.